          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We observe in Fig. 13.15 that the lines do not intersect anywhere and are parallel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.641,
            0.402,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.677,
            0.688,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you prove that two lines of equal slope are parallel?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.7,
            0.852,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Consider the equations of the two lines to be y = mx + d and y = mx + d )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.734,
            0.883,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 13:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Romila went to a stationery shop and purchased 2 erasers and 3 A4 sheets for ₹9. Her friend Sonali saw the new variety of erasers and A4 sheets Romila bought, and she also bought 4 erasers and 6 A4 sheets of the same kind for ₹18. Represent this situation graphically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.836,
            0.883,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us denote the cost of a erasers by ₹x and one A4 sheets by ₹y. Then the algebraic representation is given by the equations 2x + 3y = 9 and 4x + 6y = 18. Writing these equations in standard form we get 2x + 3y – 9 = 0 and 4x + 6y – 18 = 0."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
